**Findings**

No blocking inconsistency found. Static review indicates `dddjango` keeps the same core plugin name, skill responsibilities, reference structure, DDD standard, Django Ninja standard, and verification-honesty rules across the shared skill artifacts.

The platform-specific differences look like packaging/metadata, not divergent standards: Codex uses [dddjango/.codex-plugin/plugin.json](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/dddjango/.codex-plugin/plugin.json:2) with `"name": "dddjango"` and `skills: "./skills/"`, while the local marketplace wrapper uses [`.agents/plugins/marketplace.json`](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/.agents/plugins/marketplace.json:1) as `dddjango-local` pointing to `./plugins/dddjango`. The symlink `plugins/dddjango -> ../dddjango` matches the packaging explanation in [plugin-structure.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/workspace/docs/plugin-structure.md:111).

The common-standard contract is explicit in [plugin-structure.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/workspace/docs/plugin-structure.md:165): skill name, responsibility, reference filenames, DDD standard, Django Ninja API standard, and verification principles must remain common; platform differences are limited to packaging/metadata. The repo-local generated validation passed: `OK: validation passed with 0 warning(s)`.

DDD and Ninja standards are aligned: [spec.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/workspace/docs/spec.md:16) defines this as a Claude Code/Codex common plugin, [spec.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/workspace/docs/spec.md:20) fixes Django Ninja as the new API standard rather than DRF, [architecture-ddd/SKILL.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/dddjango/skills/architecture-ddd/SKILL.md:28) preserves strategic DDD-first rules, and [implementation-django-ninja/SKILL.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/dddjango/skills/implementation-django-ninja/SKILL.md:9) correctly marks Ninja as provisional with fallback sources instead of pretending a dedicated source reference exists.

Verification honesty is consistently present: [spec.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/workspace/docs/spec.md:81), [implementation-test/SKILL.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/dddjango/skills/implementation-test/SKILL.md:38), and [workflow-dddjango-subagents/SKILL.md](/Users/hyun/Desktop/dddjango/dddjango/skills/workflow-dddjango-subagents/SKILL.md:63) all require reporting only checks that actually ran.

